# Robot 1, auto 3 "R1 Left Wall: Wait, Launch, Park Left" (autos/LeftWallWaitLaunchAndPark.java), as RED.
# In a match our partner's shots tip the HIVE first; here four POLLEN dropped into the up CELL tip it. Then
# the CELL on the left side is up. The back on the left wall, the 3rd tile out (0.6 in off centre, clear of
# the FLOWER), facing the HIVE: wait 15 s, fire at 2325 RPM, then slide (no turn) to the left corner of our LOADING ZONE.
# Run it from the ftc-helper-lib folder: ./gradlew :sim:scenario -Pfile=../simulator/scenarios/r1-auto-left.sim
robot ../robot.properties
set scatter realistic
set piece POLLEN 18.6 -12.75 62
set piece POLLEN 18.6 -12.75 66
set piece POLLEN 18.6 -12.75 70
set piece POLLEN 18.6 -12.75 74
wait 2
expect tips "Red" >= 1                # the HIVE has tipped: the left CELL is up
init "R1 Left Wall: Wait, Launch, Park Left"
press g1.b                                 # RED
wait 0.5
expect robot x = -62 0.3
expect robot y = -11.2 0.3
expect robot heading = -90 1               # the front (the ramp) facing the HIVE
expect shape intake_arm = 85 0.1
start
wait 14
expect launched = 0                        # it waits for our partner (15 s)
expect within 25 launched >= 4
expect within 30 phase STOPPED
wait 0.5
expect screen has "Fire all at 2325 RPM: done (4 fired)"
expect screen has "To the LOADING ZONE: done"
expect screen not "skipped"
expect screen not "cut short"
expect bumped none
# Parked at the left corner of the red LOADING ZONE (x -46.6..-23.9, y up to -59.1): beside the zone,
# only the robot's corner over the zone's corner, which is a PARK; the zone stays free.
expect robot y > -57
expect robot y < -50
expect robot x > -51
expect robot x < -44
expect robot heading = -90 5
expect points "red" >= 18                  # 10 already on the field for red + LEAVE 3 + PARK 5
print robot
print pieces
expect error none
